# Legal Readiness

- Distinguish `UGC`, `licensed`, and `external-source` tracks in code
  and user-facing text.
- Never claim the service does not store audio if any `UGC` upload
  flow writes audio to DotSound storage.
- If changes touch `upload`, `import`, `playback`, `complaints`, or
  `LegalView`, review `LEGAL.md` and `docs/legal/*.md`.
- If changes affect external sources, also review
  `docs/legal/SOURCE_TERMS_CHECKLIST.md`.
- If complaint or rightsholder fields exist in schema/model, keep the
  frontend, route, service, and repository in sync.
- Treat own playback over third-party stream URLs as high-risk: do not
  expand it casually or describe it as low-risk `source-first`.
